# ============================================================================
# Python Dependencies for Portfolio Analytics Pipeline
# ============================================================================
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE:
#   pip install -r requirements.txt
#
# WHY PIN VERSIONS?
#   - Ensures consistent behavior across environments
#   - Prevents breaking changes from automatic updates
#   - Makes debugging easier (everyone has same versions)
#
# HOW TO UPDATE:
#   1. Test new version locally first
#   2. Update version number here
#   3. Test in GitHub Actions
#   4. Document any breaking changes
#
# ============================================================================

# --- DATA PROCESSING ---

# pandas: DataFrame manipulation and data analysis
# Why we need it: Clean data, feature engineering, aggregations
pandas>=2.1.0,<3.0.0

# numpy: Numerical computing (pandas dependency)
# Why we need it: Array operations, mathematical functions
numpy>=1.24.0,<2.0.0

# pyarrow: Fast columnar data format (Parquet files)
# Why we need it: Efficient storage and fast I/O for cleaned data
pyarrow>=14.0.0,<15.0.0

# --- DATABASES ---

# pymongo: MongoDB driver for Python
# Why we need it: Connect to MongoDB Atlas, query event data
pymongo>=4.6.0,<5.0.0

# redis: Redis driver for Python
# Why we need it: Cache aggregated metrics for fast dashboard queries
redis>=5.0.0,<6.0.0

# --- WEB SCRAPING / USER AGENT PARSING (Optional) ---

# user-agents: Parse user agent strings (browser/device detection)
# Why we need it: Extract device type and browser from user agent
# NOTE: batch_processor.py has simplified version if you skip this
user-agents>=2.2.0,<3.0.0

# --- UTILITIES ---

# python-dotenv: Load environment variables from .env file
# Why we need it: Local development with .env instead of exporting vars
# NOTE: Not needed in GitHub Actions (uses secrets)
python-dotenv>=1.0.0,<2.0.0

# --- DASHBOARD (if building Plotly Dash) ---

